 ## Background
-Adaptive Offset Masking was introduced in the paper "HAC++: Towards 100X Compression of 3D Gaussian Splatting" [S1]. It builds on the Gaussian Volume Mask technique [12710-gaussian-volume-mask.md] by integrating the mask into the rate calculation for adaptive updates [S1].
+The technique originates from the HAC++ paper, which introduces learnable binary masks for pruning Gaussians and anchors while integrating them into rate calculation for adaptive updates [S1]. It is applied within differentiable 3D Gaussian Splatting training pipelines to control sparsity and compression rate jointly [S1].
 
